# Code Style & Conventions

## Vue Component Structure

### Always Use `<script setup lang="ts">`
```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref, reactive } from 'vue'
import { onLoad } from '@dcloudio/uni-app'
// Component code
</script>

<template>
  <view class="container">
    <text>Content</text>
  </view>
</template>

<style scoped lang="scss">
/* Component styles */
</style>
```

### Template Structure Order
```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
// 1. Type imports
import type { User } from '@/api'

// 2. Vue APIs
import { ref, reactive, computed } from 'vue'
import { onLoad, onShow } from '@dcloudio/uni-app'

// 3. Store imports
import { useUserStore } from '@/store/user'

// 4. API imports
import apis from '@/api'

// 5. Composables & stores
const userStore = useUserStore()

// 6. Reactive data
const loading = ref(false)
const form = reactive({})

// 7. Computed properties
const displayName = computed(() => userStore.name)

// 8. Methods
function handleSubmit() { }

// 9. Lifecycle hooks
onLoad(() => { })
</script>

<template>
  <!-- uni-app tags -->
</template>

<style scoped lang="scss">
/* Prefer TailwindCSS utilities */
</style>
```

## uni-app Template Tags

### Always Use uni-app Components
```vue
<!-- ✅ Good - uni-app tags -->
<template>
  <view class="container">
    <text>Title</text>
    <image src="@/static/logo.png" mode="widthFix" />
    <button type="primary" @click="handleClick">Submit</button>
    <input v-model="value" placeholder="Enter text" />
  </view>
</template>

<!-- ❌ Bad - HTML tags -->
<template>
  <div class="container">
    <span>Title</span>
    <img src="@/static/logo.png" />
  </div>
</template>
```

### Common uni-app Tags
- `<view>` - container (like `<div>`)
- `<text>` - text (like `<span>`)
- `<image>` - images (like `<img>`)
- `<button>` - button (native)
- `<input>` - text input (native)
- `<scroll-view>` - scrollable container
- `<swiper>` - carousel
- `<navigator>` - navigation link

### @dcloudio/uni-ui Components
All uni-ui components are **auto-imported** - no need to import!

```vue
<template>
  <view>
    <!-- No import needed! -->
    <uni-icons type="heart" size="30" />
    <uni-badge text="10" type="error" />
    <uni-card title="Title" />
    <uni-list>
      <uni-list-item title="Item" />
    </uni-list>
  </view>
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
// No need to import uni-* components
</script>
```

## TypeScript Best Practices

### Type Annotations
```typescript
// Typed refs
const loading = ref<boolean>(false)
const userList = ref<User[]>([])

// Reactive objects
interface FormData {
  username: string
  password: string
}
const form = reactive<FormData>({
  username: '',
  password: ''
})

// Function types
async function login(data: LoginRequest): Promise<void> {
  await apis.auth.login(data)
}

// Interfaces
interface User {
  userId: string
  userName: string
  avatar?: string
}
```

## Imports - Always Explicit

**CRITICAL**: **Always write explicit imports** for:
- Vue APIs (ref, reactive, computed, watch)
- uni-app lifecycle hooks (onLoad, onShow, etc.)
- Types and interfaces
- Store composables
- Utility functions
- API functions

```typescript
// ✅ Good - Explicit
import { ref, reactive, computed } from 'vue'
import { onLoad, onShow } from '@dcloudio/uni-app'
import { useUserStore } from '@/store/user'
import apis, { type LoginRequest } from '@/api'

// ❌ Bad - Relying on auto-imports
const loading = ref(false)  // Where is ref from?
onLoad(() => {})  // Where is onLoad from?
```

## TailwindCSS Styling

### Prefer Utility Classes
```vue
<template>
  <!-- ✅ Good - TailwindCSS -->
  <view class="flex flex-col items-center p-[20rpx]">
    <image class="w-[200rpx] h-[200rpx] rounded-full" src="avatar.jpg" />
    <text class="text-[28rpx] font-bold">Username</text>
  </view>
</template>
```

### Use rpx Units

**CRITICAL**: In uni-app, viewport width is **always 750rpx** regardless of device screen size.

```vue
<!-- ✅ Good - rpx units (750rpx = full width) -->
<view class="w-[750rpx] h-[200rpx] text-[28rpx]">
</view>

<!-- ❌ Bad - px units (not responsive) -->
<view class="w-[375px] h-[100px] text-[14px]">
</view>
```

**Converting from Figma/Design Files**:
- Design width 375px → multiply by 2 to get rpx
- Design width 750px → use directly as rpx
- Formula: `rpx = (design_px / design_width) * 750`

Examples:
```
Figma 375px wide:       Figma 750px wide:
100px → 200rpx          200px → 200rpx
14px  → 28rpx           28px  → 28rpx
10px  → 20rpx           20px  → 20rpx
```

## Naming Conventions

### Folders & Files
- **Folders** in `/src/pages/`: kebab-case
  - ✅ `mine/`, `user-profile/`
  - ❌ `Mine/`, `UserProfile/`
- **Files**: kebab-case or `index.vue`

### Code Elements
```typescript
// Functions - camelCase
function handleLogin() { }
async function fetchUserData() { }

// Constants - UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
const API_BASE_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_APP_BASE_URL
const MAX_FILE_SIZE = 10 * 1024 * 1024

// Interfaces - PascalCase
interface UserProfile {
  id: string
  name: string
}

interface LoginForm {
  username: string
  password: string
}
```

## uni-app API Usage

### Promisified APIs

**IMPORTANT**: This project wraps uni APIs with promisify for better async/await usage. 

**Always check `/src/utils/promisify.ts` first** before using uni APIs directly!

```typescript
import { 
  showToastAsync, 
  showModalAsync,
  getStorageAsync,
  setStorageAsync,
  uploadFile,
  chooseMedia,
  previewImage
} from '@/utils/promisify'

// ✅ Good - Use promisified version
async function handleAction() {
  await showToastAsync({ title: '操作成功', icon: 'success' })
  
  const confirm = await showModalAsync({
    title: '提示',
    content: '确认删除吗？'
  })
  // Will throw if user cancels
}

// ✅ Good - Promisified storage
const userInfo = await getStorageAsync({ key: 'userInfo' })
await setStorageAsync({ key: 'userInfo', data: userInfo })

// ❌ Bad - Direct uni API with callbacks
uni.showToast({
  title: '操作成功',
  icon: 'success',
  success: () => {
    // Callback hell
  }
})
```

**Available Promisified APIs** (in `/src/utils/promisify.ts`):
- `showToastAsync`, `showModalAsync`
- `getStorageAsync`, `setStorageAsync`
- `uploadFile`, `downloadFile`
- `chooseMedia`, `chooseMessageFile`
- `previewImage`, `setClipboardData`
- `login`, `setTabBarBadge`, `removeTabBarBadge`
- `saveImageToPhotosAlbumAsync`, `saveVideoToPhotosAlbumAsync`

### Adding New Promisified APIs

If you need a uni API that's not in promisify.ts, **add it there first**:

```typescript
// /src/utils/promisify.ts

// Add new promisified API
export const chooseImage = promisify(uni.chooseImage)
export const chooseVideo = promisify(uni.chooseVideo)
export const getLocation = promisify(uni.getLocation)
```

Then use in components:
```typescript
import { chooseImage } from '@/utils/promisify'

async function selectImage() {
  const res = await chooseImage({
    count: 1,
    sizeType: ['compressed']
  })
  const filePath = res.tempFilePaths[0]
}
```

### Navigation (Direct uni API OK)
Navigation APIs don't need promisify:
```typescript
// ✅ Direct usage OK for navigation
uni.navigateTo({ url: '/pages/mine/index' })
uni.redirectTo({ url: '/pages/login' })
uni.reLaunch({ url: '/pages/index' })
uni.switchTab({ url: '/pages/index' })
```

### Loading APIs (Direct uni API OK)
Loading/hide APIs don't need promisify:
```typescript
// ✅ Direct usage OK
uni.showLoading({ title: '加载中...' })
uni.hideLoading()
```

### Network Requests
Use configured axios (not `uni.request()` directly):
```typescript
// ✅ Good - Use configured axios
import apis from '@/api'

async function fetchData() {
  const res = await apis.getData()
  return res
}

// ❌ Bad - Direct uni.request
uni.request({
  url: 'https://api.example.com/user',
  success: (res) => { }
})
```

## Lifecycle Hooks

```typescript
import { onLoad, onShow, onReady, onHide, onUnload } from '@dcloudio/uni-app'

// Page load (with query params)
onLoad((options) => {
  console.log('Loaded with:', options)
})

// Page show (every time)
onShow(() => {
  refreshData()
})

// Page ready (DOM rendered)
onReady(() => {
  // DOM operations
})

// Page hide
onHide(() => {
  // Save state
})

// Page unload
onUnload(() => {
  // Cleanup
})
```

### Pull-down Refresh
```typescript
import { onPullDownRefresh } from '@dcloudio/uni-app'

onPullDownRefresh(async () => {
  await refreshData()
  uni.stopPullDownRefresh()
})
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

1. ❌ Don't use HTML tags - use uni-app tags (`<view>`, `<text>`)
2. ❌ Don't use Web APIs - use uni APIs
3. ❌ Don't use callback-based uni APIs - use promisified versions from `/src/utils/promisify.ts`
4. ❌ Don't use px - use rpx (viewport is always 750rpx)
5. ❌ Don't use `var` - use `const` or `let`
6. ❌ Don't mutate props directly
7. ❌ Don't forget `.value` for refs
8. ❌ Don't create large components - split them
9. ❌ Don't hardcode URLs - use env variables
10. ❌ Don't use console.log in production
11. ❌ **Don't rely on auto-imports** - always write explicit imports for Vue APIs

## Security Best Practices

1. Include auth token in requests (handled by interceptor)
2. Validate user input on client and server
3. Sanitize user input in forms
4. Use permission checks for sensitive operations
5. Don't expose sensitive data in console logs
6. Use HTTPS for all API requests

